{
  "note": "The properties registry: the declaration table of docs/registries.md, binding scope x property to its one authoritative registry. Registries name their carrier, key field (structural identity, exempt from declaration), target grain, scope, gate, and whether their per-row fields are `governed` (held to the declarations below) or `ungoverned` (declared and counted, with a written `why` naming what about the carrier the field check cannot reach). Declarations carry mode (recorded or computed, with the deriver for computed), required (what the gates enforce today: value, counted, or none), and the value domain where one is closed. Governed carriers are held both ways by tools/test/properties-registry.test.mjs: an undeclared row field fails, a declared property missing from the carrier fails, a value outside a declared closed domain fails, and a required:value property blank on any row fails (2,304 presence assertions across 52 declarations; both added after audits found the same rot, that a field nothing reads goes wrong: eight domains declared and none read, then 54 value grades unchecked and three false), a computed declaration whose deriver does not exist fails, and the ungoverned count is asserted so it can only move deliberately. Expanded 2026-08-09 from six registries to thirteen by the reconciliation recorded in docs/registries.md, which walked the estate against the model rather than the model against itself. All fifteen are field-governed. Five were initially declared ungoverned with written reasons and all five reasons proved wrong on inspection, so the assertion now reads zero rather than a count: `fields: ungoverned` survives only so that adding one has to change a test. Origin: budget-drs data/design/properties.csv in mehrlander/home.",
